## 6. Prevent Information Leakage in Logs  

When logging errors, avoid printing request bodies or headers that might contain secrets (passwords, tokens). A simple pattern:

```js
function safeLogError(err, req) {
  const { method, originalUrl, ip } = req;
  console.error(`[ERROR] ${method} ${originalUrl} from ${ip}: ${err.message}`);
}
```

Replace the `console.error` in the error handler with `safeLogError(err, req)`.

