## 5. Refactor the file structure (optional but recommended)

A tiny app can stay in a single file, but as soon as you add validation, error handling, and services, splitting concerns becomes safer.

```
/src
  ├─ app.js           // express app + middleware registration
  ├─ routes/
  │    └─ health.js
  │    └─ users.js
  ├─ controllers/
  │    └─ users.controller.js
  ├─ middleware/
  │    ├─ errorHandler.js
  │    └─ validator.js
  └─ utils/
       └─ logger.js   // Winston / Pino wrapper
```

Then `app.js` simply wires everything together, making it easier to audit each piece.

